        <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:#a1a1aa;line-height:1.75;margin:0">Financial reports, government data releases, research paper appendices, and regulatory filings are commonly distributed as PDFs containing data tables that need further analysis. Manually re-typing table data from PDFs into Excel is slow and error-prone. Automated PDF-to-Excel extraction transfers the data accurately into a spreadsheet where you can apply formulas, create charts, sort, and filter. Common use cases: extracting financial statement tables, property data from government reports, pricing tables from supplier PDFs, and statistical data from research publications.</p>
